## 9. Cross-Register Note

**What differs:**

Part I describes the visual appearance of the game's range hints, while Part II explicitly defines the educational concept being taught by that same display mechanism.

**Part I says (quote):**

"When you do, I'll flash and show you two numbers in my face mask. The secret number is always somewhere *between* the two numbers I show you."

**Part II says (quote), or is silent:**

"Number Guesser helps to teach the important basic concept of *number betweeness* (the unknown secret number is always *between* the two numbers shown in DataMan's display) and number logic."

**Why this matters to an analyst:**

Part I gives the raw operational feedback from the system's interface perspective (what the display screen literally flashes to the child). Part II explains the underlying pedagogical requirement and functional domain rationale (*why* the system presents bounds rather than high/low indicators). An analyst relying solely on Part I understands the UI behavior but misses the underlying business logic and learning objectives driving feature design; relying solely on Part II provides the abstract requirement while leaving UI feedback details underspecified.

